  "question": {
    "html": "<p>An atom of hydrogen (<sup>1</sup><sub>1</sub>H) and an atom of helium (<sup>4</sup><sub>2</sub>He) are moving with the same kinetic energy.</p>\n<p>The de Broglie wavelength of the hydrogen atom is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{H}\"></span> and the de Broglie wavelength of the helium atom is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{He}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\lambda_{H}}{\\lambda_{He}}\"></span>?</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4\"></span></li></ol>"
